OpenStreetMap
-------------
The worldwide parks layer (`lib/mapdata/parks-world.json.gz`, built by
`scripts/build-parks.ts` from Overpass queries against OpenStreetMap data,
read by `lib/basemap.ts`) contains information from OpenStreetMap, made
available at openstreetmap.org under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0
(https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1.0/) — the codebase's own
attribution string (`scripts/build-parks.ts`, `lib/photobook/strings.ts`).
Because this file redistributes a static extract of the database rather
than only querying it live, that file — `lib/mapdata/parks-world.json.gz`
and any data drawn from it — is itself available under ODbL 1.0, not under
the Apache-2.0 licence that covers the rest of this repository's source.

Natural Earth
-------------
The base map (borders, water, terrain and the "famous peaks" layer in
`lib/mapdata/basemap.json.gz`, built by `scripts/build-mapdata.mjs` and read
by `lib/basemap.ts`) is built from Natural Earth (https://www.naturalearthdata.com/),
which is in the public domain. No attribution is legally required; Natural
Earth's own request is a courtesy credit of "Made with Natural Earth."

